35,2,1,talk,May,,"@Kenji, the filing rules are a nightmare. Moving it means a new notice every single time. We are stuck here unless we build something permanent.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"@May, the station block’s bin house smells worse than the open pile by midsummer. A permanent structure might just trap the heat and odor.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@May, @Mizuki, the ledger shows thirty-four thousand yen yearly just for open bags. The subsidy covers forty percent, capped at ninety thousand. We need to know if that covers the setup","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""May"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Midori,,"@May, the complaint log shows eleven of fourteen entries came from the gate household. @Mizuki, the meeting statements say nobody wants to turn bags away. We need a plan that doesn’t force us to police each other.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, the minutes show their structure bred new quarrels within two years. We must weigh the four-month filing delay against the risk of repeating their mistakes.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,May,,"@Kenji, forty percent is a drop in the bucket. @Midori, if one house files most complaints, moving it just shifts the burden. We need fairness, not just a new location.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Midori, the complaint log confirms the gate household bears the brunt. @Servas, the bin house’s trapped smell proves a permanent structure might worsen the August heat.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Midori"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@May, forty percent is helpful, but the average shelter cost is two hundred forty-eight thousand. That’s a big ask for five households. We need to be realistic about who can afford that share.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Kenji, that cost is steep. @May, the meeting showed nobody wants to police bags. We need a solution that doesn’t force us into that awkward role.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, the minutes reveal that structures breed new quarrels over maintenance. We must ask: who sweeps, and who pays for the latch?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,May,,"@Kenji, two hundred forty-eight thousand is a lot. @Midori, if we build, we need a clear, fair rule for who pays and who cleans, so nobody feels stuck with the bill.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, the subsidy helps, but the smell data is alarming. @Midori, if we build, we must ensure it doesn’t trap the heat.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@May, @Mizuki, I hear you. The subsidy helps, but the remaining cost is still heavy. We need a plan that doesn’t break the bank or our friendships.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Kenji, I hear you. @May, the meeting showed nobody wants to police bags. We need a solution that doesn’t force us into that awkward role.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
